<!--META-DATA
{
	"tags": ["dice", "poker", "reroll-policy", "function", "selection-mask"]
}
-->

<statement>
	<p>
		<pf>reroll_greedy</pf> keeps the modal face(s) in the current hand and marks all other dice for reroll. This maximizes immediate matching (e.g., push toward three-/four-/five-of-a-kind).
	</p>

	<tabular valign="top" halign="right" top="minor">
		<col width="12%"/>
		<col width="88%" halign="left"/>

		<row>
			<cell><p>Inputs:</p></cell>
			<cell>
				<p><pf>roll</pf> (1x5) integer — current dice (faces 1–6). Preferably sorted by rank.</p>
				<p><pf>counts</pf> (1x6) integer — face counts from <pf>get_face_counts</pf>.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>

		<row bottom="minor">
			<cell><p>Outputs:</p></cell>
			<cell><p><pf>sel</pf> (1x5) logical — <q>true</q> for dice to reroll; non-modal faces are marked true.</p></cell>
		</row>

		<row>
			<cell><p>Details:</p></cell>
			<cell>
				<p>▸ Let <m>m = \max(\text{counts}(\text{roll}))</m>. Any die whose face occurs fewer than <m>m</m> times is marked for reroll.</p>
				<p>▸ Ties for the mode are kept (all faces with multiplicity <m>m</m> are held).</p>
			</cell>
		</row>

		<row bottom="minor">
			<cell><p>Notes:</p></cell>
			<cell><p>▸ Works best when <pf>roll</pf> was previously standardized (e.g., via <pf>sort_by_rank</pf>).</p></cell>
		</row>
	</tabular>

	<p>
		Example:
		<program>
			<code>
				roll   = [5 5 3 2 5];
				counts = get_face_counts(roll);  % e.g., [0 1 1 0 3 0]
				sel = reroll_greedy(roll, counts)
				% Keep 5s, reroll others -> sel = [0 0 1 1 0]
			</code>
		</program>
	</p>
</statement>
